---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="References - Awesome GitHub"
  description="Primary references and source material for the Awesome GitHub site."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Sources</div>
    <h1>References</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The site keeps the citation trail short and explicit so the public material stays
      trustworthy and easy to extend.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Primary sources</h2>
    <div class="refs">
      <a class="ref" href="/wceu-2026/">
        WCEU 2026 talk page
        <span>The public entry point for the conference talk and supporting material.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="/wceu-2026/slides/">
        WCEU 2026 slides index
        <span>Browsable list of every slide page in the talk deck.</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github/blob/develop/wceu-2026/ACCESSIBILITY_AUDIT.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        Accessibility audit
        <span>WCAG checks, contrast guidance, keyboard behaviour, and delivery notes.</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github/blob/develop/wceu-2026/VISUAL_DESIGN_SPECIFICATIONS.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        Visual design specifications
        <span>Dark-mode palette, typography, spacing, and slide layout guidance.</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github/blob/develop/wceu-2026/SPEAKER_NOTES_FINAL.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        Speaker notes
        <span>Final talk narrative aligned to the slide sequence.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href="https://awesome-copilot.github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        Awesome GitHub Copilot site
        <span>Live reference for the browse-first structure and content hierarchy.</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/github/awesome-copilot/tree/main/website"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        awesome-copilot website source
        <span>Source tree used to understand the Astro and content layout patterns.</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ref" href={`${base}llms.txt`}>
        llms.txt
        <span>Machine-readable index for the public site.</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>WCEU source pack</h2>
    <div class="refs">
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github/blob/develop/wceu-2026/references/slide-to-source-mapping.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        Slide-to-source mapping
        <span>Reference map for the talk slide set and supporting repo files.</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github/blob/develop/wceu-2026/SLIDES_INDEX.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        Slide index
        <span>Inventory of the full slide set and its talking points.</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github/blob/develop/wceu-2026/ACCESSIBILITY_AUDIT.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        Accessibility audit checklist
        <span>Slide-level accessibility guidance and verification steps.</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github/blob/develop/wceu-2026/FINAL_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        Final review checklist
        <span>Launch readiness checks for the conference deck.</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="ref"
        href="https://github.com/lightspeedwp/.github/blob/develop/wceu-2026/WCEU_2026_AUDIT_AND_READINESS_PLAN.md"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        Audit and readiness plan
        <span>Broader planning path that informed the talk structure and content.</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Planning inputs</h2>
    <div class="page-copy">
      <p>
        The public copy was shaped from the planning briefs in <code>wceu-2026/website/</code>,
        the talk slides in <code>wceu-2026/slides/</code>, and the full audit and reference
        tree in <code>wceu-2026/</code>, then tightened for the live site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
